From maustin at amgen.com  Fri Mar  3 15:37:46 2006
From: maustin at amgen.com (Austin, Matt)
Date: Fri, 03 Mar 2006 07:37:46 -0800
Subject: Re: using xYplot (was: trellis line plots with error bars)
Message-ID: <E7D5AB4811D20B489622AABA9C53859109DAD909@teal-exch.amgen.com>

The trellis functions accept a 'scale' argument, so xYplot should also.

In the scale argument, you want to create a list for the y-components of the
scale and you want to set the relationship between the y-axes to be 'free'
between the different panels.

xYplot(y~x|z,  
       groups=k,
       scale=list(y=list(relation='free'))

--Matt

Matt Austin
Statistician
Amgen, Inc

